son\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6fae10dc85931da8da24ca767af5edc4d0050c4a0d56de56d37b01d22730a03b","event_uuid":"4734463e-8ba8-4494-bde3-f8f4f6399f42","position":{"commit_sha":"214ef70109846906a9215dd05971a60ce0f35ff2","position":"1787627757802104001-4734463e-8ba8-4494-bde3-f8f4f6399f42"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review advisory disposition: use the completion workflow recorder's existing per-step `duration_ms`, grouped by `step_id`, at the local completion-dispatch seam. Do not add clocks or hooks to the shared workflow interpreter/executor. Emit concrete precheck/context, completion-agent, reconcile, no-LLM passthrough, unclassified-step, and explicit residual fields; retain `verifier_workflow_ms` only as the aggregate. Compute the integer-ms residual after flooring the recorded partitions so each newly emitted record reconciles exactly; the reusable probe allows a documented 1 ms tolerance for serialization/rounding compatibility. This adds only one bounded in-memory pass over the recorder records and sidecar dictionary construction.","timestamp":1787627703548273001}],"created_at":1787626705715675001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"37302e6e-f62d-4e8c-a5ca-fc9d01e5cfd7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0538-9893-97b2-4c2d"}],"description":"## Context\nThe completion-verifier sidecar now attributes wrapper time without a residual, but the largest inner interval is still exposed only as `workflow_ms`. That label hides the operations responsible for hundreds of seconds and cannot support performance diagnosis or expectation-setting.\n\n## Plan\n- Trace the completion workflow call path and define concrete, non-overlapping subphase boundaries whose sum explains `workflow_ms`.\n- Add monotonic duration measurements at existing seams only; instrumentation must not add LLM calls, Git work, filesystem snapshots, network requests, retries, or other material work.\n- Emit the named subphase durations in the completion sidecar while preserving existing aggregate fields and compatibility with older sidecars.\n- Extend the reusable duration probe to display and validate the new workflow breakdown and surface any remaining workflow residual explicitly.\n- Add focused automated coverage for metric emission, partition arithmetic, and legacy sidecars; rely on CI for execution because local resources are limited.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `workflow_ms` is broken into concrete operation-named, non-overlapping subphase durations.\n- [ ] The subphase durations plus an explicit residual reconcile to `workflow_ms` within documented rounding tolerance.\n- [ ] Instrumentation performs only in-process monotonic clock reads and sidecar field construction; it adds no LLM, Git, filesystem snapshot, network, retry, or subprocess work.\n- [ ] Existing aggregate fields remain available and older sidecars remain parseable by the reusable probe.\n- [ ] CI coverage verifies emission and arithmetic for the new fields and compatibility for old records.\n- [ ] The final ticket record explains what each formerly generic workflow interval contains.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_metrics.py","reason":"Extract the completion metrics cluster and aggregate concrete workflow step durations without adding external work."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"Feed the existing recorder and workflow elapsed interval into the concrete phase aggregator while keeping the public aggregate."},{"path":"scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py","reason":"Name, report, and reconcile the new concrete completion workflow phases."},{"path":"scripts/rebar_duration_probe_support.py","reason":"Read the new sidecar fields while preserving older event compatibility."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation.py","reason":"Specify metric emission and partition arithmetic at the completion dispatcher seam."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_rebar_duration_probe.py","reason":"Specify probe reporting, source labels, residual handling, and legacy sidecar compatibility."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4f3b31d1-a702-42d1-a2ce-dac5e50b223e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["observability","performance","completion-verifier"],"ticket_id":"3569-58fe-4303-4b78","ticket_type":"task","title":"Break down completion verifier workflow timing into concrete subphases","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ee6266d5-f32a-4859-a337-efc619a252e8","37302e6e-f62d-4e8c-a5ca-fc9d01e5cfd7","c6f0e71b-ad6c-4fc4-96a3-e58b2cfe29b6","e8535b39-7768-4f16-8f47-c08d3656e1a1","55a514cc-d3ce-4fbc-802d-e719227aee4e","4f3b31d1-a702-42d1-a2ce-dac5e50b223e","4734463e-8ba8-4494-bde3-f8f4f6399f42"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787638207608482948,"uuid":"d92875f6-daca-42a9-8010-0d075d00b32c"}